From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mar Witek <mar@cloudflare.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 16:37:34 +0200
Subject: Disable preserve_most on Windows x64 before Clang 22

Clang versions 17 through 21 can select a register that remains live
under the preserve_most calling convention when restoring the stack in
an x86 function epilogue. This violates the calling convention and can
corrupt the caller's state.

The issue is fixed in Clang 22. Disable preserve_most on Windows x64 for
affected compiler versions while leaving other supported targets
unchanged.

See https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/pull/156817.

diff --git a/include/v8config.h b/include/v8config.h
--- a/include/v8config.h
+++ b/include/v8config.h
@@ -399,3 +399,8 @@
+// Clang <= 21 can also overwrite a live preserved register in x86 function
+// epilogues (https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/pull/156817). This manifests
+// under the Windows x64 ABI, so require clang >= 22 there.
+#if !defined(_WIN32) || __clang_major__ >= 22
 # define V8_HAS_ATTRIBUTE_PRESERVE_MOST (__has_attribute(preserve_most))
 #endif
+#endif
 # define V8_HAS_ATTRIBUTE_VISIBILITY (__has_attribute(visibility))
